	"name": "Drek",
	"type": "heritage",
	"img": "icons/creatures/abilities/cougar-pounce-stalk-black.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<h2>Drek Traits</h2><p><strong>Type:</strong> Humanoid</p><p><strong>Age:</strong> Drek grow swiftly, reaching their full height by 7 years of age, but continue to develop their physical and mental characteristics until they are roughly 20 years of age. This can become quite painful in their teen years when their adult teeth come in, and their jaw and lower skull adapt to the new, longer, teeth.</p><p><strong>Size:</strong> Medium. The overall body length, including tail, of a drek is usually 7-8ft, though their hunched posture gives them a ‘height’ of 5’8” on average.</p><p><strong>Speed:</strong> 35ft. While the Drek sometimes appear to have an ungainly gait, they are quite swift.</p><p><strong>Vision:</strong> Darkvision 60ft. Drek darkvision relies on the tapetum lucidum, which causes their eyes to glow in dim but not pitch black conditions, and a form of movement based impressions, causing drek in pitch black conditions to move their heads from side to side.</p><p><strong>Regeneration:</strong> Wounded beasts don’t live long on death planets. Once per long rest, a drek can expend a hit die as a bonus action to recover HP. When you do so, you may reattach a missing body part as per the Regenerate spell.</p><p><strong>Tail Strike:</strong> As a bonus action, you can use your tail to strike nearby targets. This natural weapon uses your Strength modifier to attack and deals 1d6 bludgeoning damage with no modifier.</p><h2>Drek Gifts</h2><h3>Jungle (Tookreh Bloodline)</h3><p><strong>Ambush Predator:</strong> You gain proficiency in the Perception and Stealth skills.</p><p><strong>Swift Climber:</strong> You gain a climb speed of 30ft and gain expertise on checks made to climb.</p><p><strong>Toxin Resistance:</strong> You have resistance to poison damage and immunity to ingested poisons and toxins.</p><h3>Saltwater (Otanreh Bloodline)</h3><p><strong>Fast Swimmer:</strong> You gain a swim speed of 30ft, and you gain expertise on checks made to swim.</p><p><strong>Deep Breaths:</strong> You can hold your breath for up to 30 minutes.</p><p><strong>Slippery when Wet:</strong> Your people had to avoid being consumed by bigger beasts, granting you expertise on checks made to escape or maintain a grapple.</p><h3>Savannah (Adareh Bloodline)</h3><p><strong>Lope:</strong> Your speed increases by +5ft.</p><p><strong>Persistence:</strong> You require only 4 hours of rest to complete a long rest and may be active for 18 hours a day without incurring fatigue.</p><p><strong>Pounce:</strong> You can use a bonus action to make a leap without provoking opportunity attacks. The distance of the leap is 5ft per point of proficiency bonus.</p><p>You may use this ability a number of times equal to your proficiency modifier and recover expended uses on a long rest.</p><h2>Drek Paragon Traits</h2><p>At 10th level, you gain an additional trait from your heritage chosen from the list below.</p><h3>Lunging Strikes</h3><p>You are able to use your hunched position and the heavy counterweight of your tail to extend your reach with melee weapons by 5ft. In addition, your swim or climb speed, if you have one, increases by 10ft. You can now recover 2 uses of Pounce on a short rest if you possess the ability.</p><h3>Lick Wounds</h3><p>When you use your regeneration heritage trait, you can now expend up to three hit dice.</p>",
